17a", "type": "topic", "title": "Lead Writing", "description": "Leads are the promise a story makes to the reader. This unit trains students to write leads that are accurate, specific, concise, and newsworthy.", "children": [{"id": "02e29fe3-6c78-4cc9-a9b8-2f2f0a0c980f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hard-news leads", "children": [{"id": "8867bce0-66b5-446f-99c9-1538cc3ce4d6", "type": "concept", "title": "who/what/when/where"}, {"id": "b60fff9f-583e-4a61-8f53-d9fc62c35936", "type": "concept", "title": "impact first"}, {"id": "01cd67ff-b6ab-4c60-af48-5a189af08b33", "type": "concept", "title": "avoid clutter"}], "description": "Students write summary leads that capture the most important verified development without overloading the sentence."}, {"id": "414b5dc7-af71-4f8b-942b-378a0a408f65", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Delayed and feature-style leads", "children": [{"id": "58932e44-6bbc-4a81-a8ce-a01801b8650e", "type": "concept", "title": "anecdotal leads"}, {"id": "66051944-e8e4-48b5-9237-5f0312b021b8", "type": "concept", "title": "scene leads"}, {"id": "cc43a425-7d46-4da2-b203-f47017ee0eba", "type": "concept", "title": "nut graf connection"}], "description": "The unit introduces when a delayed lead is appropriate and when it weakens basic news."}, {"id": "d0a1c165-a1a7-48ef-bdb6-d191d6430232", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lead revision", "children": [{"id": "d99cc59e-f8d5-483c-ab2f-8c13c97b8ce8", "type": "concept", "title": "buried news"}, {"id": "309659cf-3484-4324-a536-7819c95660a7", "type": "concept", "title": "false emphasis"}, {"id": "5700ee24-e066-4d9f-b3e6-7a5ac26c6f22", "type": "concept", "title": "precision"}], "description": "Students diagnose vague, buried, overwritten, or unsupported leads."}]}, {"id": "3269955d-5664-4fb2-8fbb-3d375d1dff8c", "type": "topic", "title": "Interviewing Basics", "description": "Interviewing is a reporting method, not just a conversation. Students learn to prepare, listen, follow up, and treat sources ethically.", "children": [{"id": "a9881410-8827-41ae-a363-f6e524f10134", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interview preparation", "children": [{"id": "acdb9198-c538-4b69-a047-bb93e3d974f1", "type": "concept", "title": "background research"}, {"id": "b402870e-b006-4794-bf50-ebbe4162c9b0", "type": "concept", "title": "question ladder"}, {"id": "32cd7fd7-1e88-4642-960a-45eef6c89eeb", "type": "concept", "title": "source purpose"}], "description": "Students research the source, topic, and likely information gaps before asking questions."}, {"id": "6505bf00-dc4e-467b-8e92-051e82e7601c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Questioning and listening", "children": [{"id": "5c94c02f-2ccb-42be-9fce-8ffff76d31cf", "type": "concept", "title": "open-ended questions"}, {"id": "95bf6738-ac41-43d0-8e4f-8242eb024d9f", "type": "concept", "title": "follow-ups"}, {"id": "2e1f9417-5597-4ab4-8ae5-a19e90643a4c", "type": "concept", "title": "clarifying questions"}], "description": "The unit emphasizes open questions, precise follow-ups, silence, and active listening."}, {"id": "dcc57c04-be2b-4563-97cc-8f71077613cf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interview ethics", "children": [{"id": "b8eee4f4-9a5b-499e-a653-c6dd94a7bd1a", "type": "concept", "title": "informed interaction"}, {"id": "91923ef1-745c-4af1-bc7a-6f85a92ec63c", "type": "concept", "title": "minors"}, {"id": "8b17ff4a-93ca-4095-871f-9a61c0c51634", "type": "concept", "title": "trauma awareness"}], "description": "Students learn how to identify themselves, handle vulnerable sources, and avoid deception or coercion."}]}, {"id": "d243f671-62bd-4cf9-9f2e-463a45f2295a", "type": "topic", "title": "Source Mapping and Beat Reporting Basics", "description": "Even beginning stories need more than one voice. This unit helps students build source lists and understand communities, institutions, and beats.", "children": [{"id": "ac842419-0c01-48cb-b89d-b9396d7e5b84", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Source diversity", "children": [{"id": "633f3735-d87f-4c49-a14e-7e759a3bbf08", "type": "concept", "title": "official sources"}, {"id": "8c45c396-d71e-462b-8c0d-616e0973cb69", "type": "concept", "title": "affected people"}, {"id": "3fdccdc0-a65f-4e89-9b4d-e8b838477da3", "type": "concept", "title": "expert sources"}], "description": "Students learn to avoid relying only on officials or the most convenient voices."}, {"id": "b0bdef90-df1a-48a0-9654-30c296de5fb5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Beat mapping", "children": [{"id": "53308436-ca9b-44eb-af17-77732f70e0c0", "type": "concept", "title": "stakeholders"}, {"id": "3498e180-1e1f-4418-9dc2-6820133891b9", "type": "concept", "title": "calendar events"}, {"id": "67f38089-7d77-4651-8d2b-399a50af93ef", "type": "concept", "title": "public agencies"}], "description": "Students map people, institutions, records, meetings, and recurring issues on a small beat."}, {"id": "8e85d5e1-772a-44ae-ace7-dbd1a15b8cf1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Source relationships", "children": [{"id": "4b667551-016c-4be2-b965-269ab5d9ee1c", "type": "concept", "title": "contact logs"}, {"id": "2273c4a2-2d32-4b5b-a8bb-3c7a09b8aedf", "type": "concept", "title": "boundaries"}, {"id": "ef053165-4c17-49d7-81f1-8dbe58507483", "type": "concept", "title": "ongoing questions"}], "description": "The class introduces professional boundaries, trust, independence, and follow-up routines."}]}, {"id": "fcca2706-adeb-4968-a62c-d97e7bf0bc98", "type": "topic", "title": "Attribution and Quotes", "description": "Attribution tells readers how journalists know what they know. Students learn to use quotes and paraphrases accurately and transparently.", "children": [{"id": "64e10534-ddcd-4d28-9be2-a3dc022ee415", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Attribution fundamentals", "children": [{"id": "96ca3553-929a-41ef-ac79-5ea6090ad3a9", "type": "concept", "title": "said"}, {"id": "e5dc2cff-d51b-41b0-8b16-b6f95fd6057c", "type": "concept", "title": "according to"}, {"id": "b88a4bb9-bd44-4f66-b11e-f34f6e3182aa", "type": "concept", "title": "source clarity"}], "description": "Students practice when to attribute, how often to attribute, and where attribution belongs in a sentence."}, {"id": "bdf97a3a-6133-418b-b8be-0559c1efa438", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quote selection", "children": [{"id": "a780a1aa-489c-43da-827c-7b3b02aab69f", "type": "concept", "title": "direct quotes"}, {"id": "25844f0b-bb1c-4d71-b2b1-475f7fc832b1", "type": "concept", "title": "partial quotes"}, {"id": "f367be39-90c7-4fe5-bd0a-a661fd01adad", "type": "concept", "title": "quote trimming"}], "description": "The unit teaches students to quote language that is distinctive, revealing, or evidentiary rather than routine."}, {"id": "d7b78da4-76fa-4d4b-aff7-7473720f3d41", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Paraphrase and context", "children": [{"id": "2813b057-99de-4da2-af0e-f3e75aa63a70", "type": "concept", "title": "context"}, {"id": "51b75461-e039-44f3-ae60-97670d94babe", "type": "concept", "title": "accuracy"}, {"id": "3f5c7585-c4ca-4fbf-9761-439265cb397f", "type": "concept", "title": "misquotation risk"}], "description": "Students learn to paraphrase fairly and avoid changing meaning when simplifying language."}]}, {"id": "122e7ca6-6c7f-429a-8bbb-c2e6e13cd0bd", "type": "topic", "title": "AP Style and Newsroom Mechanics", "description": "AP style gives beginning reporters a shared newsroom language for consistency, readability, and professional polish.", "children": [{"id": "c754dce6-b85c-412d-9d3c-ab52929a7ddc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AP style essentials", "children": [{"id": "11b64aa9-60a0-42fa-9607-ef2d371e521c", "type": "concept", "title": "names and titles"}, {"id": "78b1bd8d-88f1-4ec4-8226-b8d2cd274044", "type": "concept", "title": "numbers"}, {"id": "8d31d94e-1030-4135-8868-c94794d67a79", "type": "concept", "title": "dates"}, {"id": "3eb77e30-6e36-422c-b8f5-ed835d365456", "type": "concept", "title": "addresses"}], "description": "Students practice the style rules most likely to appear in first news assignments."}, {"id": "03ed2162-4d8e-479c-b3c2-e0f4e31713ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Grammar for news clarity", "children": [{"id": "3af61718-ab9f-4409-b98a-c79c5490e9fe", "type": "concept", "title": "subject-verb agreement"}, {"id": "0be44572-b254-46e4-a096-5ebc495c716d", "type": "concept", "title": "modifiers"}, {"id": "1629aa81-fcfa-406d-956a-1402bb79f9a9", "type": "concept", "title": "punctuation"}], "description": "The unit reviews mechanics that can change meaning or weaken authority."}, {"id": "e760b157-cdb3-4f76-8f62-60980d5037e7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Copy preparation", "children": [{"id": "5a40f416-2882-43bf-8a44-e10bf87de499", "type": "concept", "title": "slugs"}, {"id": "eb907341-4c9e-4acd-ac34-bc00a703591f", "type": "concept", "title": "bylines"}, {"id": "27cbb2e6-ddfe-47ec-9efd-3536de7f3aad", "type": "concept", "title": "datelines"}, {"id": "e6f73381-35f3-4382-8c27-c1a1f992f7cc", "type": "concept", "title": "file naming"}], "description": "Students learn basic newsroom conventions for clean copy before editing."}]}, {"id": "f26bd212-8f58-4706-ba5d-e5232e56fdb5", "type": "topic", "title": "Verification, Accuracy, and Fact-Checking", "description": "Verification is the discipline that separates journalism from rumor. Students learn practical accuracy routines before publication.", "children": [{"id": "5d1b5550-3784-4c47-b4a1-81ce3c110e97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accuracy checklist", "children": [{"id": "b0f60566-e17f-4d8b-a85c-c8b23c57ca3f", "type": "concept", "title": "proper nouns"}, {"id": "c0157067-ba51-4c00-9bed-495f6d93d0a1", "type": "concept", "title": "numbers"}, {"id": "42ea2dfb-e1fe-4522-9cbd-ba4441f3a370", "type": "concept", "title": "chronology"}], "description": "Students check names, titles, dates, places, numbers, links, and claims before filing."}, {"id": "c9aff8a6-9839-4a9e-a097-cb7c829d01e6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Triangulating information", "children": [{"id": "dda750d3-4edf-4688-a534-01757e1f530d", "type": "concept", "title": "multiple sources"}, {"id": "55617c95-28dd-4f1e-bc41-487faf347bdb", "type": "concept", "title": "document checks"}, {"id": "ddc2c1a4-16c8-4085-9a66-9dc42c2fefd4", "type": "concept", "title": "conflicting accounts"}], "description": "The class introduces how to compare interviews, documents, observation, and official records."}, {"id": "e4e09ea3-094a-46d2-b36e-1604e7a0acec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Corrections and transparency", "children": [{"id": "a8b18fbd-397e-45e3-a23a-d08c887fd757", "type": "concept", "title": "updates"}, {"id": "00ab46ed-eda9-4e02-b7d3-c26af798dd3b", "type": "concept", "title": "correction language"}, {"id": "d9218935-11ce-40b6-b204-de1562fcda49", "type": "concept", "title": "accountability"}], "description": "Students learn what to do when information changes or an error is discovered."}]}, {"id": "20227e83-4d62-46ec-b7cb-47a02c6b1daf", "type": "topic", "title": "Documents, Public Records, and Basic Research", "description": "Beginning reporters need to know that not every fact comes from an interview. This unit introduces documents as reporting evidence.", "children": [{"id": "2c2100b0-7ea3-4518-9aa7-3d2fb2c9f780", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Finding basic documents", "children": [{"id": "45a9196b-07d3-48bb-89ff-9c03e5d4816e", "type": "concept", "title": "public agendas"}, {"id": "9abe35bd-050c-4f12-84e1-418728a3f915", "type": "concept", "title": "budgets"}, {"id": "f180ddff-d890-412d-b1f6-4f420e7ccaed", "type": "concept", "title": "reports"}], "description": "Students learn where to look for agendas, budgets, reports, court records, police logs, and campus documents."}, {"id": "8f37b4d4-858a-43fc-ae67-8aaebc5366ca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reading documents for story ideas", "children": [{"id": "daffb997-7a6d-499d-8b49-462e119ac8e9", "type": "concept", "title": "what changed"}, {"id": "5d87078b-4364-46c8-82b3-863a45c74a11", "type": "concept", "title": "who is affected"}, {"id": "5920b584-b9ca-4040-ae3a-e7989f977e67", "type": "concept", "title": "what is missing"}], "description": "The unit teaches students to identify news, anomalies, and unanswered questions in records."}, {"id": "3c779f5d-2903-41d9-be90-58082b6dc269", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using research responsibly", "children": [{"id": "4f57f75e-0cd3-4357-80ea-e24b7d32d9bd", "type": "concept", "title": "document context"}, {"id": "98ebe95c-d658-4826-afd9-16aa0adabaf4", "type": "concept", "title": "linking"}], "description": "Students learn to cite, attribute, and verify documents without overclaiming."}]}, {"id": "e39dc866-acbd-4ff6-be62-b429b9c3515e", "type": "topic", "title": "Covering Speeches, Events, and Meetings", "description": "Meetings and speeches are classic first assignments because they demand preparation, listening, quick judgment, and accurate summary.", "children": [{"id": "97e63c88-0ef7-4f4b-bd93-14dd8ff32edc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Before the event", "children": [{"id": "ada96b31-efb0-4b83-a70a-c80ca2168c27", "type": "concept", "title": "agenda review"}, {"id": "09e316be-b7fe-48b4-9001-be5bac20cae9", "type": "concept", "title": "background clips"}, {"id": "d7f92d95-6685-410f-8e2d-76fc97b2fa56", "type": "concept", "title": "source list"}], "description": "Students learn to read agendas, identify stakeholders, and anticipate likely news before arriving."}, {"id": "fa2c0d4a-cc4d-4a2f-aeef-f6200a64c114", "type": "subtopic", "title": "During the event", "children": [{"id": "cc95c173-7b6f-4e97-b34b-1bac1e50e528", "type": "concept", "title": "live notes"}, {"id": "889beb65-f0ae-408f-97e5-9d8ad55d27a3", "type": "concept", "title": "motions and votes"}, {"id": "de9f8bd8-e3ac-464f-80a3-2b9dba5c6dcc", "type": "concept", "title": "audience reaction"}], "description": "The class practices note-taking, quote capture, chronology, and distinguishing news from routine proceedings."}, {"id": "1bcae71b-3a27-448d-994e-b4df0ba146cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "After the event", "children": [{"id": "6ceb2d0d-cad3-4779-8c15-5ff6cddcd36f", "type": "concept", "title": "post-event interviews"}, {"id": "b6bf5dc5-76a0-4bb2-8df6-46b26632055e", "type": "concept", "title": "missing context"}, {"id": "1d4006d2-c808-4a59-b1f9-8f1591eb7c42", "type": "concept", "title": "deadline filing"}], "description": "Students learn to follow up, verify details, and write a story that is more than a transcript."}]}, {"id": "6bf8c77b-4607-4ee1-8cad-465ecf82dff2", "type": "topic", "title": "Writing on Deadline", "description": "Deadline writing teaches students to make good-enough decisions under real constraints while keeping accuracy first.", "children": [{"id": "d149d408-a586-4beb-9bc7-e72b71a865c1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deadline workflow", "children": [{"id": "63d3cbc0-d0a9-4d09-85b7-bd85f36de0ed", "type": "concept", "title": "time budgeting"}, {"id": "62778822-4a47-43b6-8881-7fb28ae3ba8f", "type": "concept", "title": "minimum viable story"}, {"id": "44789330-3567-444c-8f82-05f6ec4f9e3c", "type": "concept", "title": "filing order"}], "description": "Students practice reporting, outlining, drafting, revising, and filing in a compressed window."}, {"id": "7f300493-cf0f-4528-bfe5-01524be26fb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prioritizing under pressure", "children": [{"id": "10bea5ab-90fb-41f4-a365-7529df59be5a", "type": "concept", "title": "must-have facts"}, {"id": "f0bd2599-f522-4395-9e8f-837bebf87b55", "type": "concept", "title": "risk triage"}, {"id": "f6f5e453-0978-4b3c-a557-37e44fe7a89a", "type": "concept", "title": "second-day angles"}], "description": "The unit teaches students what must be verified now and what can wait for a follow-up."}, {"id": "334272b5-dae7-4167-9c85-511d400bef19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clean, fast revision", "children": [{"id": "021e3f98-1222-4897-8af1-0cc96a5f57b9", "type": "concept", "title": "top edit"}, {"id": "314deb6c-406e-4054-8cd5-15015fc3c363", "type": "concept", "title": "fact pass"}, {"id": "b2a47699-8bb5-4e32-be82-56981a74f109", "type": "concept", "title": "style pass"}], "description": "Students revise for clarity, accuracy, and structure without endlessly polishing."}]}, {"id": "31628c66-ac02-4a75-8a21-2b494ab34ba4", "type": "topic", "title": "Writing for Digital, Mobile, and Social Contexts", "description": "Even a first reporting course should prepare students to file for readers who encounter news on phones, search, newsletters, and social platforms.", "children": [{"id": "63627258-e20d-400b-bd95-6b1ebfb10b90", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital story basics", "children": [{"id": "f8a06edc-370f-4383-98e4-68348742ebc9", "type": "concept", "title": "links"}, {"id": "248b4d99-eea8-4dcd-a262-ff40c25034d7", "type": "concept", "title": "captions"}, {"id": "dcc22a2a-6454-4780-8aaf-2bcde7f7ac06", "type": "concept", "title": "tags"}], "description": "Students learn how links, embeds, photos, captions, and metadata support a basic news story."}, {"id": "ff06f8f4-d552-489f-9e26-f1e67715abbb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mobile readability", "children": [{"id": "a63c3816-76fc-434c-9a7d-0b8160167452", "type": "concept", "title": "paragraph length"}, {"id": "3493c002-4ba9-4577-a2d4-fe9c9bbff49c", "type": "concept", "title": "subheads"}, {"id": "f1cdfa62-40f7-4a6e-acda-e673c1e76623", "type": "concept", "title": "context blocks"}], "description": "The unit emphasizes short paragraphs, clear structure, useful context, and scannable updates."}, {"id": "e780d5f2-546f-4544-bcfb-dd3ff475f5d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social reporting caution", "children": [{"id": "c8c95912-7062-41ee-92de-fd23273a36cb", "type": "concept", "title": "source discovery"}, {"id": "b64c11b3-8cf1-402d-b018-547be84bfb72", "type": "concept", "title": "screenshots"}, {"id": "26c69c4d-25d0-4749-a4fc-eddaeca7364e", "type": "concept", "title": "verification before amplification"}], "description": "Students learn to use social media for discovery while verifying before publication."}]}, {"id": "3a0b46ab-6296-40bb-b449-1f28c7668976", "type": "topic", "title": "Community, Fairness, and Inclusive Reporting", "description": "World-class introductory reporting teaches students that accuracy includes fairness, context, representation, and awareness of harm.", "children": [{"id": "8417e5b4-3fe0-4660-be5f-a8d8673ef7bb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fairness and right of response", "children": [{"id": "6bb9b8d4-23a4-475c-b3cc-698ff5584d9d", "type": "concept", "title": "response requests"}, {"id": "c72d4818-b557-4bb0-a197-3b46033cd31b", "type": "concept", "title": "time limits"}, {"id": "b9e7d90e-31b5-4b42-bea1-9332b01e73dd", "type": "concept", "title": "no comment"}], "description": "Students learn to give people a meaningful chance to respond to claims that affect them."}, {"id": "96c2778b-ff78-4ecf-b1e1-5ed10efab1a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive sourcing", "children": [{"id": "379b7ac7-75a7-4cb4-8173-f45536b58434", "type": "concept", "title": "source gaps"}, {"id": "46e748be-3053-4949-b2c3-fc9fce754113", "type": "concept", "title": "community voices"}, {"id": "2295e72a-4607-4741-8fd7-802f34268838", "type": "concept", "title": "language access"}], "description": "The unit asks students to notice whose perspectives are missing and why."}, {"id": "f27af7c5-d668-4e39-8aa4-6b6f973e6a76", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sensitive reporting", "children": [{"id": "929136da-95e2-4606-95b3-d5f7db839e18", "type": "concept", "title": "harm minimization"}, {"id": "6fa7e59f-2093-427b-9757-48a292a33eba", "type": "concept", "title": "identity relevance"}, {"id": "6d3432aa-ede6-44e1-b777-ea77bd9e64fd", "type": "concept", "title": "stereotype avoidance"}], "description": "Students practice respectful language and careful framing for trauma, identity, crime, and vulnerable communities."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$nwr1json$::jsonb,
